Objective:
Remove the blue styling from the top of the mobile app.

1. Check app/layout.js (Metadata):

    Look for the viewport export or metadata export.
    Change the themeColor from the current blue (e.g., #2563eb) to black (#000000) or the dark grey background color (#121212). This will fix the blue status bar on iOS.

2. Check app/layout.js (HTML):

    Look inside the <body> tag.
    If there is a <div> or <nav> with bg-blue-XXX or bg-primary wrapping the {children}, remove that background class or the element entirely.

3. Check app/globals.css:

    Check if the :root variable --background or --foreground is set to a blue color.

4. Fix the Dashboard Centering (Recap):

    In app/page.js, ensure the main container for the cards has mx-auto and max-w-md (or similar) to center it on the screen.

Please check these specific files and remove the blue styling.